The repository owns one MCQ standard and one evidence tracker. For MCQ work, read
the relevant sections of `docs/mcq-quality-standard.md` and
`docs/mcq-quality/workflow.md`; for a corpus-wide continuation use
`PROMPT_PLAN_INTERVIEW.md` and `PLAN_INTERVIEW.md`. For a theory-only edit, follow
the Markdown conventions and check whether the paired MCQ became stale.

Use `python3 scripts/mcq-workflow.py status --topic <topic>` for one topic or
`next --size 4` for the queue. Review the visible Markdown question, every Q/B,
all A/B/C/D and their sections. Check facts, SFPL, ANSC and natural Russian
separately. Automated form signals do not grant editorial PASS.

After changes, run the relevant gates. Register independent two-phase results
through `record`, then update `checkpoint` or `sync` at a control point.
Keep accepted unchanged blocks and the user's existing edits intact.
